From f4450fe92c10ea2fd0e3a8679260c30870527588 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vlad Syan <vlad.syan@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 10:54:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] Plane: add RFSEARCH mode (AUTO with RF sweeps)

RFSEARCH (mode 27, "RFSR") flies the mission like AUTO; it is mode_auto with
a flag, so every AUTO check (take-off, landing, failsafes, fence) still
applies. A companion sends its analyzer reading as NAMED_VALUE_FLOAT RF_dBm.
On a plain waypoint leg, when the smoothed reading is at least RFS_THR_DBM,
the plane sweeps its nose antenna: by default one full-bank circle (RFS_TYPE
2 right, 1 left; 0 = left/right legs to RFS_LEG_DEG, extended while the
signal rises), rolling out onto the leg. Sweeps repeat every RFS_SPACING
while each sweep peaks above RFS_THR_DBM - RFS_STOP_DB. No sweeps during
take-off, landing, failsafe or within RFS_MIN_LEG of a waypoint; a landing
or failsafe entry into AUTO clears the flag.

The sweep phase goes to the companion as NAMED_VALUE_FLOAT RFS_SWP and is
logged as RFS. Tested in SITL only, with a synthetic companion.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
